BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Royal Conservatory Orchestra with Conductor Earl Lee
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260501T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260501T200000
UID:988949b1ae1c04e076651e909bc97cae@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:A renowned Korean-Canadian cellist and conductor\, currently M
 usic Director of the Ann Arbor Symphony. He also served as assistant condu
 ctor of the Boston Symphony\, resident conductor of the Toronto Symphony O
 rchestra\, and associate conductor of the Pittsburgh Symphony. He is the 2
 022 recipient of The Sir Georg Solti Conducting Award. The Temerty Orchest
 ral Program at The Glenn Gould School\, the Royal Conservatory Orchestra i
 s widely regarded as an outstanding ensemble and one of the best training 
 orchestras in North America\, with graduates having joined the ranks of th
 e greatest orchestras in the world. Please join us! This concert is preced
 ed by a short performance by talented students of The Royal Conservatory.
LOCATION:Koerner Hall\, Royal Conservatory of Music\, 273 Bloor St W\, Tor
 onto\, ON
URL:https://www.rcmusic.com/Tickets/Seats/378401
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
