BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gather for Doors Open at Spadina Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T100000
UID:cdab6988cbeb33bce938c6377a08a903@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Spadina Museum tells the stories of the affluent Austin family
 \, those who worked in their service\, and of the transformational changes
  in Toronto in the 1920s. At Spadina Museum visitors are invited to engage
  with the site at their own pace and to bring their questions and curiosit
 y. This year's theme for Doors Open is The World in a City and at Spadina 
 Museum visitors will find elements of gathering\, sports and play througho
 ut\, exploring the sports\, games and leisure activities enjoyed in the 19
 20s. Visitors are invited to enjoy the 6 acres of lush gardens surrounding
  the home.
LOCATION:Spadina Museum\, 285 Spadina Rd\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/spadi
 na-museum/
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Prepare The Ground 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260529T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T180000
UID:46151d6f6f7fcea51fe1ece528fa554c@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:A community-led arts and heavy music festival\, the first of i
 ts kind in the city! Founded by two lifelong friends\, Toronto-based conce
 rt promoter Denholm Whale and KW Campol of music management company Mythos
  and the Perpetual Flame Ministries record label/art house. Drawing inspir
 ation from European festival stalwarts like Roadburn\, Supersonic\, and Am
 plifest\, we're focused on heavy music as an ethos of collective catharsis
  more than a dedication to one specific metal subgenre. From burgeoning ar
 tists\, to favorites you never thought would reunite\, to one-off full alb
 um sets\, a heavily curated and meticulously planned lineup is the festiva
 l's key component.
LOCATION:Trinity St Paul's\, 427 Bloor St W\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://link.dice.fm/u82686a23a97?dice_id=u82686a23a97
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Penn and Teller: 50 Years of Magic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T200000
UID:aee7417132ec404b1d273b0035712cda@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Amazing magic. Tremendous trickery. Hilarious antics. Get read
 y to have your mind blown! Watch as the world's most legendary magicians\,
  Pen and Teller celebrate their milestone anniversary. The celebrated duo 
 will blend classic favourites with astonishing new illusions\, all deliver
 ed with their trademark wit and showmanship for an unforgettable live expe
 rience. David Letterman lauds them as "evil geniuses—always amazing\, al
 ways entertaining\," while The New York Times hails their act as "a wither
 ingly funny\, brazen assault on the temple of magic\," and The Times of Lo
 ndon declares that "the comedy-magic duo are at their absolute peak:.
LOCATION:Meridian Hall\, 1 Front St E\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://www.luminatofestival.com/PennTeller
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:10 Days in a Madhouse
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T133000
UID:cb25416e41e72c88db60fe9e73757346@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Is she insane\, or just pretending? In this gripping psycholog
 ical opera based on true events from 1887\, trailblazing reporter Nellie B
 ly fakes madness to expose the truth from inside New York's notorious Blac
 kwell's Asylum. What she discovers is a world where women are silenced\, s
 anity is questioned\, and power decides who is believed. This Canadian pre
 miere from composer Rene Orth and librettist Hannah Moscovitch stars Mirei
 lle Asselin as Nellie Bly and Jorell Williams as Dr. Blackwell. Directed b
 y Joanna Settle (Sky on Swings)\, 10 Days in a Madhouse boasts an evocativ
 e set by Andrew Lieberman that transforms the asylum into a maze of the mi
 nd. Composed by Rene Orth with a libretto by Hannah Moscovitch\, 10 Days i
 n a Madhouse is directed by Joanna Settle (Sky on Swings). Designer Andrew
  Lieberman's set transforms the asylum into a maze of the mind.
LOCATION:Bluma Appel Theatre\, 27 Front St E\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://am.ticketmaster.com/tolive/10daysinamadhouse-lum2026
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Los Callejeros Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T100000
UID:2e4118eb01b3554b2f4e16f475f2e661@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Explore selections from works reflecting Jim Bravo's memories 
 of his early immigrant inner-city experiences\, and correlated interpretat
 ions of our sublime Canadian landscape. This exhibition adds yet another v
 oice to the developing story and renewed global interest surrounding quest
 ions of race and immigration witnessed in society recently. About the Arti
 st Jim Bravo was born in Ecuador\, South America\, and is of Afro-Latino a
 nd Quichua descent. He emigrated to Toronto Canada with his family in the 
 mid 70s and spent his youth in the downtown central west and east core of 
 the city. He is a graduate of The Ontario College of Art and Design Univer
 sity where he majored in Fine Art and public monumental painting. A multi 
 award winning painter including first honor for the prestigious 2023 Kings
 ton Prize For Contemporary Canadian Portraiture\, Bravo is also the recipi
 ent of grants from Toronto Art Council\, Ontario Arts Council grants and T
 ABIA Mural Award.
LOCATION:Assembly Hall Gallery\, 1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr\, Etobicok
 e\, ON
URL:www.jimbravopaintings.weebly.com
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Play Dead
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T160000
UID:495db7d93771795f1d9f61e3994ddf88@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Play Dead invites you into a distorted world where the familia
 r twists into something wonderful and strange. Everyday rituals warp into 
 surreal scenes\, exposing the desperation that underpins our search for co
 nnection. In this gravity-defying universe\, bodies collide and tangle\, c
 aught between beauty and menace — both intimate and unsettling. Montreal
 's People Watching crafts a vivid blend of acrobatics\, movement\, and hig
 h octane circus that magnifies the absurdity of the everyday. These moment
 s\, strange yet achingly familiar\, mirror our own desire to hold on\, lik
 e couples not wanting the last dance to end. Haunting and exhilarating\, P
 lay Dead captures the fragility\, absurdity\, and fleeting wonder of life 
 lived on the edge of connection. La Presse lauds the performance as "Maste
 rful fluidity\, breathtaking…the circus of tomorrow".
LOCATION:Meridian Arts Centre\, 5040 Yonge St\, North York\, ON
URL:https://www.luminatofestival.com/play-dead
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
